.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MKDIR 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mkdir
.Nd create visible directories
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl p
.Ar directory ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Create each directory through this process's writable filesystem view.
.Fl p
also creates missing parents and accepts an existing directory.
Without it, an existing directory is an error.
There are no mode or owner arguments.
Options precede operands; a later option word is a path.
.Ql --
ends option processing; use it or a
.Ql ./
prefix for a name beginning with a dash.
Unknown leading options return status 2.
.Pp
Creation failures are diagnosed on standard error; later operands are
attempted.
There is no rollback of directories already created.
Success prints nothing.
The command cannot change the session's mount table or write through a
read-only binding.
See
.Xr sync 1
for the file-server durability barrier.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when all directories were created or accepted by -p; 1 for failure;
2 for no operands or an unknown leading option.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mkdir -p /home/operator/notes/drafts
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rm 1 ,
.Xr sync 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
